# Sensor Changelog: Minimum Stack Hierarchy Cleanup

Date: 2026-06-17
Branch: current workspace changes

## Summary

Refined the ROS 2 package layout toward a minimum viable stack that stays
simple today while leaving room for modular growth later. This update removes a
redundant launch alias, makes `robot.launch.py` the only supported bring-up
entry point, and moves developed sensor assets into clearer subsystem-oriented
locations.

## Launch Entry Point Simplification

The supported robot startup path is now:

```bash
ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics robot.launch.py
```

Removed:

```text
launch/master.launch.py
```

`master.launch.py` had become only a compatibility wrapper around
`robot.launch.py`. Since the team is no longer using the old command, removing
the alias reduces launch surface area and keeps the bring-up story easier to
remember.

## Minimum Viable Package Hierarchy

The package now follows a leaner structure:

```text
config/
docs/
launch/
nodes/
nodes/sensors/
scripts/
```

This keeps the package small while still separating:

- launch entry points
- runtime configuration
- developed ROS nodes by subsystem
- project documentation

No empty future-facing subsystem folders were added in this pass.

## Sensor Asset Relocation

Moved:

```text
sensor/webcam/publish_apriltag_pose.py -> nodes/sensors/apriltag_pose_node.py
sensor/webcam/webcam_calibration.yaml -> config/webcam_calibration.yaml
launch/master.launch.py -> launch/robot.launch.py
```

This aligns the repo better with a ROS-native layout:

- node executables live under `nodes/`
- calibration and runtime defaults live under `config/`
- robot bring-up lives under `launch/`

## Build And Launch Wiring Updates

Updated:

```text
CMakeLists.txt
launch/sensors.launch.py
README.md
docs/setup.md
```

Changes:

- install path now points at `nodes/sensors/apriltag_pose_node.py`
- sensor launch now runs `apriltag_pose_node.py`
- setup docs now point at `robot.launch.py`
- README now reflects the new hierarchy and launch command

## Cleanup

Removed stale generated cache directories so deleted paths do not remain in the
tree as leftovers from previous runs.

Removed:

```text
sensor/
launch/__pycache__/
```

## Validation

The hierarchy cleanup was verified with:

```bash
colcon build --packages-select jmu_lunabotics --symlink-install
ros2 launch jmu_lunabotics robot.launch.py --show-args
```

Because ROS 2 launch logging tries to write under `~/.ros/log`, launch argument
verification in the sandbox was run with `ROS_LOG_DIR` redirected to `/tmp`.
